disney plus has become a massive success  thanks largely in part to its almost  complete catalog of marvel cinematic  universe movies  as well as introductions of some  fantastic original series  now tom hiddleston is returning to the  mcu as loki  and he has everything we know about his  disney plus series  so far it's been almost two years since  the announcement of the loki series  which has dragged on forever as we've  awaited the highly anticipated project  for quite a while it looked like we'll  be getting the series debut on june 11th  in keeping with the tradition of  launching disney plus series on friday  in may of 2021 though star tom  hiddleston  announced that the six episode series  will actually debut june 9th  making it the first wednesday debut on  the streaming service  wednesdays are the new fridays for now  it doesn't look like disney plus will be  changing their episode drop times  so die hard fans in the united states  will have to continue to wake up early  or stay up late for the 3am eastern  premieres  regardless of the time loki will be the  show of the summer for sure  and if its disney plus predecessors are  any indication  it should be a massive hit for marvel  studios  will there be a second season maybe  deadline all but confirmed a loki season  2  when reporting on producer michael  waldron signing a new deal  with marvel studios waldron is the  executive producer on loki and will be  petting the script for the new star wars  film  that studio head kevin feige is  producing he's also expected to return  for season 2 of the disney plus series  as a part of his contract  this could also mean that initial  reports of a 12 episode loki series  were actually indicating 12 episodes  total spread out across  two seasons marvel studios producer nate  moore also seemed to confirm more  low-key adventures  as he explained in an interview with  slash film i think there's a lot of  storytelling in loki  that's really irreverent and clever and  cool but also lends itself to multiple  seasons  in a way where it's not a one-off in  other words while no one as straight-up  officially said there will be a loki  season 2  it's looking very likely and we can't  wait to watch your six episodes to get a  better understanding  of where the show could go a series  about loki just wouldn't work without  tom hiddleston  so we're happy to report that the  charming actor will be reprising his  role as a god of mischief  but when it comes to who will be  starring alongside him there are some  pretty stellar names on the cast list  including one beloved comedy star owen  wilson has been confirmed to be  portraying  m mobius a manager in the time variants  authority  in the comics mobius is a tva bureaucrat  in charge of taking care of time  and if you disrupt the proper flow he'll  make sure to throw the book at you  even if you're a member of a powerful  superhero team or an asgardian legend  as the case may be as for the series  from what we can tell by the trailer  mobius appears to be a major character  in loki he will be working alongside the  tricks to guard  to fix the timelines he interrupted when  stealing the tesseract  interestingly this isn't the first time  that hiddleston and wilson have acted  alongside each other  and in a project involving time travel  no less the two stars appeared together  in 2011's midnight in paris  which found wilson as a modern-day  tourist accidentally stumbling into  1920s paris  where he encounters hiddleston's f scott  fitzgerald  so who else is filling out the cast of  loki well it looks like goo goo and  batara will be playing a powerful member  of the time variance authority  known as judge ren slayer from the  trailers we can tell she's obviously a  force to be reckoned with  sitting behind a large imposing desk and  looking down on loki  and chances are good that judge ren  slayer is actually ravana renslayer  a character who hails from the 40th  century and is romantically linked with  kang the conqueror  a character who'll be showing up in  ant-man and the wasp quantum mania very  soon  loki will also feature erica coleman as  florence schaffner  if that name sounds familiar it's  because schaffner was a real-life flight  attendant  involved in the infamous db cooper  hijacking and  based on the trailers it looks like old  db might actually be everybody's  favorite trickster guard  we also know that one mi masaku will be  playing a heavily armored tva officer  and we see her escort loki through a  portal in one of the trailers  masaku will be joined by sasha lane who  also seems to be playing an armored tva  agent who will most likely be giving  loki a hard time  in march 2020 variety reported that  richard e grant most famous for his  roles in with nail and i  gosford park and can you ever forgive me  was joining the cast of loki  grant's role is still being kept under  wraps but we know that he'll show up in  at least one episode  there were no obvious appearances of  grant in any of the loki trailers or  sneak peeks  so we'll have to wait till the show  debuts on june 11th  to see what his mysterious character is  up to however some fans suspect he might  be showing up as an older version  of the titular tricks to god sophia di  martino has also been confirmed for loki  and the actress known for roles  in yesterday and into the badlands is  playing another mysterious role in the  mcu project  some redditors believe she's playing  either a female version of loki  or even the evil asgardian sorceress  known as enchantress  but neither have been confirmed at this  time if you're wondering about the  behind the scenes talent  michael waldron wrote all six episodes  of loki and he also serves as an  executive producer on the series  the show is directed by kate herron who  will also serve as an executive producer  alongside kevin feige and stephen  brassard fans of the mcu should be super  excited for this experienced creative  team  and some of the loki actors are paying  respect to those on the other side of  the camera  google and bartholo praised heron on her  mcu directorial debut  in an interview with the big ticket  podcast saying i feel like even though  you're dealing with this big universe  she still makes it feel very intimate  she just brings it back down to  character and moments and emotions  for almost two years we've speculated  about what the plot for loki could  entail  and in true marvel cinematic universe  fashion mum was the word on what the  series would be about  but with the release of trailers and  sneak peeks we have a better  understanding of what to expect from  loki this  june kevin feige confirmed at san diego  comic-con in 2019  that the series would take place  immediately after the trickster stole  the tesseract  in avengers end game the trailers have  confirmed that by making off with the  space stone  loki screwed up a whole bunch of  timelines and the series will watch him  fix these broken timelines while being  guided by the time variant's authority  unbelievable wherever you go it's just  death destruction the literal  ends of worlds from the trailers we saw  loki and mobius in pompeii  so we do know the pair will be traveling  back in time as far back as 79 a.d  what other eras loki might find himself  in remains a mystery  but he's also suspected to be on earth  somewhere in 1971  based on the db cooper hints in the  trailer loki appears to be the famous  hijacker who held a plane ransom for 200  thousand dollars  and disappeared via parachute never to  be seen again  mcu projects rely heavily on the source  material and loki will be no exception  and we can make our best guesses on  which comic issues the series will pull  from based on what we saw  in the trailers there definitely will be  inspiration from 2016's vote loki  which was a satire on the united states  presidential election of the same year  loki can be seen in the trailer wearing  a pin that saves vote loki  while others around him also don the  campaign accessory  and since the time variants authority  will play a major role in the show  we know several aspects will be pulled  from the comics regarding the  organization  the tva first appeared in thor issue 371  in 1986  and the group has had encounters with a  handful of famous marvel names  including the fantastic four kang the  conqueror and she hulk  characters we all know are showing up in  the mcu sooner  rather than later the marvel cinematic  universe has one giant web of  interconnecting plots  and you can expect loki to follow suit  it hasn't been confirmed at this time  but some believe tom hiddleston will  show up as loki  in the upcoming thor loving thunder film  with him ending back up with his brother  due to the events of the disney plus  series  since the mercurial villain is confirmed  to be traveling through time and  realities  he very well could return to the main  timeline on earth and space with his  brother  we also expect loki to connect to doctor  strange in the multiverse of madness  which will delve heavily into alternate  realities that play a part in one  division  and possibly the upcoming spider-man no  way home  in an interview with bloomberg  businessweek kevin feige noted that the  events of loki and the doctor strange  sequel  will be connected doctor strange in the  multiverse of madness  is set to premiere on march 25 2022  with thor love and thunder following on  may 6 2022  it's very possible loki shows up in the  doctor strange sequel  possibly running into steven strange or  the scarlet witch  in another reality if either helps bring  him back to the main timeline  it's likely the opening for loki to  waltz into the events of thor 4  like nothing had ever happened check out  one of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

